6. 📈 Auto Scaling

Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of EC2 servers according to demand.

Example:

Normal traffic:

EC2
EC2

Heavy traffic:

EC2
EC2
EC2
EC2
EC2

Traffic decreases:

EC2
EC2

AWS can automatically add/remove instances.

Simple Example

Suppose your website normally needs:

2 servers

But during a sale:

10,000 users

Auto Scaling can do:

2 EC2
 ↓
CPU becomes high
 ↓
Add EC2
 ↓
3 EC2
 ↓
4 EC2
 ↓
